@@ -0,0 +1,24 @@
+---
+id: dl-004-classify-sub-day-rentals-as-hourly-periods
+type: decision-log
+title: "Classify sub-day rentals as hourly periods"
+status: pending
+format: 1
+---
+
+## Context
+
+The service previously accepted only whole UTC-day rental periods. The rental desk now needs to quote,
+book, and find availability for short rentals while retaining daily pricing for day-based rentals.
+
+## Decision
+
+Treat a period with midnight UTC boundaries as a day rental. Treat a period shorter than 24 hours with
+both boundaries on a UTC hour as an hourly rental. Hourly quotes and bookings require `hourlyPrice`, and
+hourly availability excludes equipment without one. Reject all other periods.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Daily behaviour and its pricing remain unchanged. Hourly bookings use the existing half-open overlap
+rule, so adjacent hourly and daily bookings remain available. A 24-hour period not bounded by midnight is
+not a supported rental period.
